======================================================================
Union H-spectrum n<=6 and the forbidden frontier through the mod-8 lens
======================================================================
realized (union n<=6): [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 37, 41, 43, 45]
odd integers in [1,45] NEVER realized at n<=6: [7, 21, 35, 39]
Note the documented universal-forbidden values:
    7 = 8*0+7  -> residue 7 mod 8;  floor(7/8)=0  (triangular!)
   21 = 8*2+5  -> residue 5 mod 8;  floor(21/8)=2

Interpretation: H is odd (residues 1,3,5,7). The 'octal peel' floor(H/8)
is the analogue of T_k for odd squares (which are exactly residue 1).
If realized H clustered at residue 1 the analogy would be tight; the data
above shows the ACTUAL residue distribution -- report it honestly.

